LOCATION:Pantokrator summit / Strinilas\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:From 1 to 6 August pilgrims climb to the monastery on the 906 m summit of Pantokrator for the six days of the Transfiguration\, sleeping in the cells and celebrating the liturgy at dawn on the 6th\; the villages below — Strinilas\, Perivoli\, Spartylas\, Palaiochori in Lefkimmi\, Agios Matthaios — hold their own panigiria on the evening of the 5th or 6th. Strinilas\, the last village before the summit road\, is the one with tavernas and music.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#pantokrator-summit-strinilas-six-day-pilgrimage-to-pantokrat
